//! Struct-layout mirrors for the pinned libgpod build, generated by bindgen
//! from the *installed* headers. Do not hand-edit the struct definitions; if
//! a field is needed that is not mirrored here, regenerate (command below).
//!
//! # Pin and provenance
//!
//! - libgpod **0.8.3**: sourceforge tarball sha256
//!   `638a7959d04e95f1e62abad02bd33702e4e8dfef98485ac7d9d50395c37e955d`
//!   plus the 8-patch set of Arch `libgpod 0.8.3-20` (packaging commit
//!   `a74dc08b`). Build recipe, patch hashes, and the dependency matrix:
//!   itl-player `docs/LIBGPOD.md`.
//! - Generated from the installed public header
//!   `include/gpod-1.0/gpod/itdb.h` of that build. Verified identical
//!   (`diff`) to the patched source tree's `src/itdb.h` it was built from.
//! - Types referenced only through pointers (`Itdb_Device`, `Itdb_Thumb`,
//!   `Itdb_Chapterdata`, the private structs) are opaque placeholders here —
//!   the wrapper never dereferences them, it only passes pointers to libgpod
//!   functions.
//! - Function declarations are deliberately absent: the typed, documented
//!   symbol set lives in `super::mod` (`ffi/mod.rs`).
//!
//! # Regeneration
//!
//! ```text
//! # in itl-player docs/LIBGPOD.md territory: the pinned build installed at
//! # $GPOD_PREFIX (default /tmp/opencode/libgpod-install)
//! cd /tmp/opencode/bindgen-gen   # throwaway project, not in any repo
//! cargo run --release -- /tmp/opencode/layouts_raw.rs
//! # then: replace the bindgen banner with this header, re-add the trailing
//! # "__BindgenOpaqueArray8" doc block, and update
//! # src/ffi/layouts_sha.rs with `sha256sum` of the final file
//! ```
//!
//! The generator (`/tmp/opencode/bindgen-gen/src/main.rs`) allowlists
//! `Itdb_iTunesDB`, `Itdb_Track`, `Itdb_Playlist`, `Itdb_Artwork`,
//! `Itdb_IpodInfo`, `Itdb_SPLPref`, `Itdb_SPLRule`, `Itdb_SPLRules`, `GList`,
//! `GError`; opaques the pointer-only types; ignores functions; and enables
//! the compile-time layout assertions you see at the bottom of this file.
//!
//! # Layout guarantees
//!
//! - Every mirrored struct carries `#[repr(C)]` plus inline `offset_of!`
//!   assertions generated from the same headers — a struct that drifts from
//!   the pinned build fails compilation, not just runtime.
//! - The ABI marker (`rufin-libgpod.abi`) ties this file's SHA-256 (see
//!   `src/ffi/layouts_sha.rs`) to the loaded library: a present-but-mismatched
//!   marker is a hard `BackendUnavailable` (crate root docs).
//! - These layouts are LP64 (64-bit Linux). `time_t` is `c_long` (i64); the
//!   enums are C `int`/`uint` widths. A 32-bit or non-Linux backend is out of
//!   scope until the packaging follow-up (`deltas/b007_delta.md` §5).
//!
//! # Sanity cross-check (one-time, 2026-11-08)
//!
//! A C probe (`itl-player/tools/libgpod_offsets.c`) compiled against the same
//! installed headers printed `offsetof` for every field the session reads;
//! all values matched these mirrors. Recorded output: `Itdb_Track` size 640,
//! `title` 8, `id` 216, `size` 220, `volume` 256, `soundcheck` 260,
//! `time_played` 280, `rating` 292, `dbid` 336, `explicit_flag` 386,
//! `skipcount` 396, `artwork` 520, `mhii_link` 528; `Itdb_iTunesDB` size 104,
//! `tracks` 0, `device` 24, `version` 32, `id` 40; `Itdb_Playlist` size 224,
//! `type` 16, `members` 24; `Itdb_Artwork` size 120, `thumbnail` 0;
//! `Itdb_IpodInfo` size 56, `ipod_model` 16; `GList` size 24; `GError`
//! size 16.

#![allow(
    dead_code,
    non_camel_case_types,
    non_snake_case,
    non_upper_case_globals
)]
// Generated doc comments quote bare URLs from the libgpod headers
// (ipodlinux.org etc.); rustdoc's bare-url lint is not actionable here.
#![allow(rustdoc::bare_urls)]
#[derive(PartialEq, Eq, Copy, Clone, Debug, Hash)]
#[repr(C, align(8))]
pub struct __BindgenOpaqueArray8<T>(pub T);
impl<T: Copy + Default, const N: usize> Default for __BindgenOpaqueArray8<[T; N]> {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Self([<T as Default>::default(); N])
    }
}
